WEBVTT

00:02.480 --> 00:05.460
<i>A warm May morning where the winds brush my cheeks.</i>

00:05.980 --> 00:08.060
<i>The trees glisten in the sunlight,</i>

00:08.820 --> 00:10.940
<i>and if you listen very closely,</i>

00:13.280 --> 00:16.740
<i>you can hear birds chirping from within.</i>

00:19.360 --> 00:20.830
Water's boiled!

00:22.660 --> 00:26.050
<i>It's been one whole month since we moved here.</i>

00:26.050 --> 00:28.080
<i>We've gotten used to our new life,</i>

00:28.080 --> 00:30.590
<i>and every day has been fun!</i>

00:32.060 --> 00:34.510
Hina, help me with these!

00:36.090 --> 00:38.100
Do not call me by that name!

00:38.100 --> 00:40.660
G-Gotcha, <i>Strarf</i>...

00:41.920 --> 00:43.850
but really, can ya lend a hand?

00:43.850 --> 00:46.110
I do not partake in such mundane tasks.

00:46.110 --> 00:48.830
C'mon, you helped out with our cooking!

00:48.830 --> 00:51.570
You made some octopus balls, remember?

00:51.570 --> 00:53.130
Silence, pest!

00:54.340 --> 00:58.090
Strarf has also become part of the family to us.

00:58.090 --> 01:01.060
Now, we all call each other buddies!

01:02.510 --> 01:05.370
And we'll finish with a good luck charm!

01:05.860 --> 01:09.740
<i>Every day begins with Lene's homemade English tea.</i>

01:10.690 --> 01:12.130
I'm gonna be late!

01:13.330 --> 01:15.300
I've got work, so I'll be out late!

01:20.060 --> 01:21.760
What <i>is</i> this?

01:21.760 --> 01:24.140
A little more good luck than usual. {lit. Something good will definitely happen to you today!}

01:24.140 --> 01:25.660
Oh?

01:26.090 --> 01:27.650
Thanks.

01:27.650 --> 01:28.730
Well, I'm off.

01:29.720 --> 01:31.980
Have a nice day, Master!

01:36.740 --> 01:36.860
<b>Ann's Diary.</b>

01:36.860 --> 01:38.490
<b>Ann's Diary.</b>

01:39.020 --> 01:41.180
<i>Master is as handsome as ever! {Lene's saying something in the background that sounds like fawning over Master, but it's not CC'd and I'm not sure it's important.}</i>

01:42.990 --> 01:42.990
{OP}

01:43.450 --> 01:45.880
It shines

01:45.880 --> 01:49.940
My singing voice is endless

01:49.940 --> 01:56.520
My eternal pledge is only for you

01:56.520 --> 02:03.260
I wonder if you're your usual self

02:03.260 --> 02:08.740
I'll sparkle with you

02:08.740 --> 02:11.750
Install dream

02:16.640 --> 02:21.630
The arms of the clock advance

02:22.860 --> 02:28.050
and with them so does time

02:28.050 --> 02:35.210
When you are sad, I open my tiny arms

02:35.210 --> 02:41.560
and embrace you

02:43.570 --> 02:45.890
Fly

02:45.890 --> 02:50.160
My singing voice is tender

02:50.160 --> 02:56.540
I can remember your shape

02:56.540 --> 02:59.540
and that wasn't brought about by a program

02:59.540 --> 03:03.160
Let us experience

03:03.160 --> 03:08.840
the turmoil in my heart together

03:08.840 --> 03:11.910
Install dream

03:13.250 --> 03:17.510
Clash! Battle Trike!

03:13.250 --> 03:17.510
Clash! Battle Trike!

03:13.250 --> 03:17.510
Clash! Battle Trike!

03:13.820 --> 03:19.050
And now, we present the final match of the previous Busou Shinki World Championship.

03:32.180 --> 03:33.570
Wow...

03:33.570 --> 03:35.710
So that's how strong the Strarf models are...

03:39.030 --> 03:42.030
Do you want to fight like that Strarf?

03:44.530 --> 03:46.300
Heeeey!

03:51.980 --> 03:55.870
Oh look, Katsura Armor! {I don't know what Katsura armor is, and googling it only results in a 2ch ep 3 livestream thread where people either w'd or asked what it was.}

03:55.870 --> 03:57.410
R-Really?

03:57.410 --> 03:59.550
Whoah, that's some cool armor!

04:03.830 --> 04:06.100
Now wait just a minute!

04:06.850 --> 04:08.060
You ignored me.

04:08.060 --> 04:11.070
I saw you glance at me, and then you totally snubbed me!

04:11.070 --> 04:14.490
Hmm... it's coming to me... {lit. This should be my area of expertise...}

04:14.900 --> 04:15.620
Thug Girl?

04:15.620 --> 04:16.860
No!

04:20.490 --> 04:22.290
It's you!

04:22.290 --> 04:24.360
What's wrong?

04:26.150 --> 04:28.760
What a chilling coincidence!

04:28.760 --> 04:33.210
The Strarf that I fought in last year's World Championship was...

04:33.830 --> 04:35.710
the same model as you!

04:40.810 --> 04:41.830
So, um...

04:41.830 --> 04:44.900
this is your first meeting?

04:45.730 --> 04:46.550
W-Well, yeah.

04:47.550 --> 04:49.560
Let us have a mock battle.

04:59.190 --> 05:01.440
I-I'm letting you off for today.

05:01.770 --> 05:02.430
She's running away?

05:02.430 --> 05:03.570
She chickened out.

05:06.060 --> 05:08.080
So, what'd ya come for?

05:08.080 --> 05:11.080
I've got something to discuss with you all.

05:11.080 --> 05:12.380
Discuss?

05:11.900 --> 05:14.120
And now, the latest on the Shinki Snatcher.

05:14.740 --> 05:17.040
Good timing. The news is covering this.

05:14.740 --> 05:17.590
{*Can't make it out beginning of sentence, ends with 神姫が盗まれる事件が相次ぐ中}

05:19.600 --> 05:22.090
The Snatcher struck again last night, sneaking into a Shinki shop in Enohama,

05:22.090 --> 05:29.100
and stealing 30 Shinkis and over 200 Shinki Parts.

05:30.350 --> 05:31.740
A Shinki thief?

05:31.740 --> 05:35.100
Yeah. He could be after every Shinki shop in town.

05:35.450 --> 05:39.810
So I'm gathering muscle to take the law into our own hands.

05:40.520 --> 05:42.610
I'd be happy to let you all join.

05:42.610 --> 05:45.360
We don't need your permission.

05:45.360 --> 05:46.280
What are you saying?

05:46.820 --> 05:49.910
Our fellow Shinkis are being plundered by pure evil!

05:50.440 --> 05:53.100
While a lone Shinki may be weak,

05:53.100 --> 05:57.120
if we combine our strength, we can fight for justice!

05:57.720 --> 05:59.130
You wish to enter combat?

05:59.130 --> 06:01.230
I've got just the thing for you, Strarf!

06:01.230 --> 06:03.130
I spent all night on it!

06:07.810 --> 06:09.090
Entering combath!

06:12.350 --> 06:13.890
Fine, geez!

06:14.220 --> 06:17.970
I was stupid to even <i>think</i> of letting you join my justice squad!

06:17.970 --> 06:18.650
Halt.

06:20.420 --> 06:22.020
I'm intrigued.

06:22.020 --> 06:23.150
I will join you.

06:33.260 --> 06:35.600
You required muscle for this? {lit. So this is the duty of a bodyguard? I already used muscle earlier, it'd be weird to switch terminology.}

06:38.260 --> 06:42.420
Vigilantes are supposed to patrol the streets at night with wooden clappers.

06:42.420 --> 06:44.050
That's how it's always been.

06:44.050 --> 06:48.700
Would such noise not reveal our position to the enemy?

06:48.700 --> 06:53.180
Oh, but it's supposed to! This is where we'll make our stand.

07:06.990 --> 07:09.090
That's <i>not</i> how you use those.

07:14.590 --> 07:16.970
The temperature's perfect... {2lewd}

07:18.740 --> 07:21.710
I wonder if Strarf's okay...

07:21.710 --> 07:24.580
Eh, who cares.

07:24.580 --> 07:26.510
She wanted to go.

07:26.790 --> 07:30.500
And she'd get more done with that nutjob than we could.

07:31.800 --> 07:35.510
Oh, Ann! I'll wash your body for you.

07:35.510 --> 07:36.510
Huh?

07:36.510 --> 07:40.020
Um, I can handle... it...

07:40.020 --> 07:41.650
Oh, hush now.

07:44.310 --> 07:45.980
It feels good...

07:46.570 --> 07:48.530
Oh, this is <i>hard</i> to clean...

07:50.150 --> 07:52.000
Th-That's cold!

07:52.000 --> 07:53.860
Come now, bear with it.

07:55.540 --> 08:00.390
It's a lady's duty to be clean down to her last screw hole. {Now this is what I call fanservice}

08:01.670 --> 08:04.000
N-Not there!

08:04.000 --> 08:07.170
S-Sto—wah!

08:15.300 --> 08:16.930
Shinki Parts?

08:22.030 --> 08:23.390
What's with this?

08:29.050 --> 08:32.340
Can you remind me what we're doing with all these Parts?

08:32.340 --> 08:36.910
I spotted 'em lying around in an abandoned apartment building!

08:38.360 --> 08:39.780
With this as our bait,

08:39.780 --> 08:45.060
we'll teach that greeting-less, housewarming soba-less rat who ignored us for a whole month

08:45.060 --> 08:46.420
a little lesson in being neighborly!

08:47.980 --> 08:50.690
Ooh, that Part looks pretty pricey!

08:50.690 --> 08:51.920
I'd like to get my paws on that!

08:52.930 --> 08:54.390
You're barking up the wrong tree!

08:59.430 --> 09:01.970
Did you not hear a scream just now?

09:01.970 --> 09:03.990
Dunno. Sure you're not hearing things?

09:11.440 --> 09:13.110
He's pretty suspicious.

09:13.110 --> 09:14.340
Let's tail him.

09:22.330 --> 09:26.080
There's only one thing to do when getting out of the bath!

09:26.080 --> 09:28.690
No, table tennis is for the hot springs.

09:28.690 --> 09:30.760
We're at an indoor bath, so we need this!

09:32.980 --> 09:35.470
All right! Grab your bottle in your right hand,

09:36.100 --> 09:38.350
legs shoulder-width apart,

09:38.920 --> 09:41.600
place your left hand on your hips, and drink!

09:46.900 --> 09:50.210
When ya hit my age, ya gotta have liquor.

09:50.210 --> 09:52.130
That's a luxury, sir.

09:54.210 --> 09:58.160
He's so obviously suspicious. He's got to be the culprit!

10:27.820 --> 10:31.470
I can't <i>believe</i> we still have such filthy vending machines!

10:34.520 --> 10:35.490
What's up?

10:36.380 --> 10:37.850
Another suspicious enemy.

10:37.850 --> 10:38.700
Another one?

10:41.860 --> 10:43.620
The Shinki shop...

10:43.620 --> 10:46.370
Seems like we've got a bingo this time.

11:00.330 --> 11:01.260
Anything there?

11:02.000 --> 11:02.890
Nothing.

11:17.750 --> 11:20.240
Hina's been out pretty late...

11:20.240 --> 11:22.890
Master is late too...

11:22.890 --> 11:26.250
His work should have ended a while ago...

11:30.530 --> 11:31.750
Got it!

11:32.860 --> 11:34.420
Hello? Ann speaking.

11:35.130 --> 11:37.000
Master! How are you?

11:37.000 --> 11:40.580
I got into a bit of trouble,

11:40.580 --> 11:42.510
and it doesn't look like I'll make it back...

11:47.860 --> 11:49.000
As I thought...

11:49.000 --> 11:50.350
we aren't alone.

11:59.780 --> 12:01.160
Master's at the police station?

12:01.160 --> 12:05.060
They found him walking with a large bundle of Shinki Parts,

12:05.060 --> 12:06.620
so they took him in for questioning.

12:06.620 --> 12:09.920
They were apparently reported of a robbery in the area...

12:09.920 --> 12:11.620
Master is the Shinki Snatcher?!

12:11.620 --> 12:15.500
Absolutely not! Master would never do such a thing!

12:15.500 --> 12:17.000
It must be a false charge!

12:18.380 --> 12:22.010
W-Well, yeah, but what about Master?

12:22.690 --> 12:26.010
He said that he'd be held there until the charges against him were cleared.

12:26.010 --> 12:30.020
That means that there's only one way for us to save Master!

12:30.340 --> 12:31.290
Yes...

12:31.290 --> 12:36.270
We'll combine forces with Strarf and find the real criminal!

12:47.470 --> 12:49.440
We're attacking. Are you ready?

12:51.400 --> 12:55.750
Once we're done with this fight, I'll give you that match you asked for.

12:57.310 --> 13:01.800
My, such words are grossly unfit for the battlefield, are they not?

13:01.800 --> 13:04.260
Way to trigger your death flag.

13:28.730 --> 13:32.500
My elegant weaponry will beat you into scrap!

13:33.280 --> 13:36.290
We'll take out anyone who gets in our Master's way!

13:36.290 --> 13:39.500
That's what we call love! {~desu wa}

13:39.500 --> 13:41.850
I'll finish you in five seconds flat!

13:41.850 --> 13:44.010
This place'll make a nice graveyard for you!

13:44.400 --> 13:46.470
Such words are also...

13:46.470 --> 13:48.180
unfit for the battlefield!

13:53.350 --> 13:55.640
Might you be my next target?

14:00.880 --> 14:01.730
Wait, Yda!

14:02.120 --> 14:03.570
I'll defeat her!

14:03.570 --> 14:06.070
I'll do it even if I go down in flames!

14:06.070 --> 14:10.700
Is there nothing you can do to reign in that pointlessly ardent nature of yours, Ach?

14:10.700 --> 14:12.870
There's no such thing as a pointless love in this world!

14:12.870 --> 14:15.710
Neither is there a pointless justice!

14:16.710 --> 14:18.380
I suppose it was foolish of me to ask.

14:18.380 --> 14:20.210
In that case, we'll fight together.

14:20.520 --> 14:21.590
Here we go!

14:38.940 --> 14:40.220
Over there!

14:48.220 --> 14:49.700
Watch it!

14:50.580 --> 14:51.910
The Shinki thief!

14:51.910 --> 14:56.290
I'll head inside! You two follow that man!

14:56.290 --> 14:57.000
Roger!

15:56.320 --> 15:57.380
Ann!

15:57.380 --> 15:59.270
Two on one is no fair!

15:59.270 --> 16:03.270
Well then, shall we have a duel, fair and square?

16:10.740 --> 16:12.240
I accept!

16:19.400 --> 16:21.230
I'll be your opponent!

16:21.230 --> 16:23.880
I'll punish you in Master's stead!

16:23.880 --> 16:25.070
Punish?

16:25.070 --> 16:26.130
W-Wait—

16:26.130 --> 16:27.670
No excuses! {mondou muyou, kind of hard to hear.}

17:02.820 --> 17:05.140
Can you keep up with my speed?

17:22.590 --> 17:24.840
My, you're not half bad.

17:24.840 --> 17:27.730
However, your fighting style lacks beauty!

17:28.290 --> 17:31.030
You must be more magnificent! More gorgeous!

17:48.140 --> 17:50.310
I don't have a grudge against you...

17:50.310 --> 17:51.380
but...

17:51.380 --> 17:54.630
if we don't catch the true criminal, then Master will—

18:06.560 --> 18:08.560
This isn't over...

18:09.690 --> 18:11.570
you evil Shinki!

18:12.320 --> 18:13.820
E-Evil?

18:13.820 --> 18:15.140
You heard me.

18:15.140 --> 18:20.710
Protecting my Master from the forces of evil, down to my last breath...

18:20.710 --> 18:22.330
is my duty!

18:25.120 --> 18:28.080
Stop this. You two were tricked.

18:28.660 --> 18:31.590
Your master left here long ago.

18:50.230 --> 18:52.610
Your attacks focus solely on style.

18:52.890 --> 18:54.030
You lack substance!

18:55.400 --> 18:56.570
Wait, Strarf!

19:01.690 --> 19:04.080
Yda! We're done here!

19:04.410 --> 19:06.460
There's no point in fighting any longer!

19:06.460 --> 19:08.600
Do you plan to double-cross me, Ach?!

19:08.600 --> 19:11.190
These Shinkis are servants of the Shinki thief!

19:11.190 --> 19:12.590
They're not.

19:13.090 --> 19:17.590
The real servants of the Shinki thief... are us.

19:26.670 --> 19:32.660
We were activated by the Shinki thief, and tricked into fighting for him.

19:35.790 --> 19:38.110
Aines and Lene sent a tip.

19:39.300 --> 19:40.770
Let's go, Yda.

19:40.770 --> 19:43.400
We know the truth now, so there's no point in staying here.

19:43.400 --> 19:45.370
Hold it! Are you trying to run away?

19:46.720 --> 19:48.150
We're not running.

19:48.150 --> 19:49.390
We're going on a journey.

19:50.790 --> 19:56.130
A journey to find true love, true justice, and the master we were created to meet!

19:56.130 --> 19:58.130
Huh? A journey?

19:59.110 --> 20:01.140
Yda, let's hurry!

20:01.140 --> 20:02.340
Understood.

20:04.390 --> 20:08.490
One day, when we find a suitable master,

20:09.020 --> 20:11.360
let us have another match!

20:13.440 --> 20:14.800
We're leaving.

20:14.800 --> 20:15.500
I'm with you!

20:22.970 --> 20:25.090
So uh, how is this all ending?

20:25.090 --> 20:30.870
I don't know, but I hope they find their perfect master someday!

20:33.820 --> 20:35.980
What an awful day...

20:35.980 --> 20:38.340
My everywhere hurts...

20:38.710 --> 20:41.230
Let me see your wounds. I'll lick them for you.

20:41.230 --> 20:46.010
This is all their fault! We'll get even, cat's honor!

20:49.770 --> 20:52.560
Why?!

20:53.920 --> 20:55.560
I'm home.

20:55.560 --> 20:58.350
Welcome home, Master!

20:58.350 --> 21:00.340
Talk about a long day...

21:00.340 --> 21:02.570
I can't believe I got mistaken for a thief!

21:03.420 --> 21:06.430
But it's a good thing the charges were dropped!

21:06.430 --> 21:11.130
Yeah. Apparently, the real criminal was caught by some Shinki...

21:12.080 --> 21:14.090
Wait, you mean...

21:14.770 --> 21:16.470
You should thank Strarf.

21:17.130 --> 21:18.340
Hina?

21:18.850 --> 21:22.340
I-It was nothing. I did not fight for Master's sake.

21:36.680 --> 21:38.300
Thank you, Hina.

21:39.210 --> 21:41.590
But don't push yourself too hard.

21:42.860 --> 21:45.060
I did not push myself...

21:45.600 --> 21:47.260
I was simply negligent.

21:50.870 --> 21:52.380
Lucky her.

21:52.380 --> 21:54.870
I'd like a coat of paint, too!

21:56.440 --> 21:59.130
But you didn't even fight!

21:59.130 --> 22:02.380
I got a scratch when I fell over earlier!

22:03.760 --> 22:06.490
Hey, I've got plenty of those!

22:09.720 --> 22:17.650
{ED}

22:19.980 --> 22:26.490
I stand here reflected in your eyes

22:26.490 --> 22:31.740
and make something of a foolish face

22:32.870 --> 22:39.330
Being more gentle than the wind and invincible like the clouds

22:39.330 --> 22:44.300
I want to protect you

22:45.420 --> 22:51.850
Here in the forest I am lost in

22:51.850 --> 22:57.560
I want to try finding a four-leaf clover

22:57.560 --> 23:04.690
The sun is guiding me

23:04.690 --> 23:10.410
towards the miracles of two stars together

23:10.410 --> 23:13.620
Even if we are hurt on the way

23:13.620 --> 23:17.580
and ten years pass

23:17.580 --> 23:24.090
this future where I can be with you is what I choose

23:24.090 --> 23:25.800
We will walk on ahead

23:27.130 --> 23:30.720
and not miss the sun's sign

23:40.780 --> 23:44.980
Hina's special treatment ticks me off! I want Master to fix my wounds, too!

23:44.980 --> 23:48.850
I know, if we just tear off our paint jobs...

23:48.850 --> 23:50.630
Whoah Ann, where are you shaving?

23:50.630 --> 23:53.450
Well then, I can shave my paint off too!

23:53.450 --> 23:55.000
Hey, so can I!

23:55.000 --> 23:56.760
Lenient... far too lenient...

23:56.760 --> 24:00.460
Next time, we'll have an action packed race battle, all for Strarf!

24:00.460 --> 24:01.900
Next time, on Busou Shinki!

24:01.040 --> 24:09.630
Next time

24:01.040 --> 24:09.630
Next time

24:01.040 --> 24:09.630
Next time

24:01.040 --> 24:09.630
"It's a Race! One Lap Around the Park!"

24:01.040 --> 24:09.630
"It's a Race! One Lap Around the Park!"

24:01.040 --> 24:09.630
"It's a Race! One Lap Around the Park!"

24:01.900 --> 24:04.700
"It's a Race! One Lap Around the Park!"

24:04.700 --> 24:06.170
One lap around the park?

24:06.170 --> 24:08.010
Strarf's getting into this...
